{title:Merry Go Round}
{subtitle:Andrew DeFaria}
{duration:3:13}
{musicpath:Music/Merry Go Round.mp3}
{key:D}

{c:Verse 1}

Painted ponies on a wooden floor,
Waiting by the ticket gate once more.
The nickel drops, the brass ring gleams,
Waking up inside the oldest dreams.
Round and round the platform spins,
Not quite sure where the journey begins.
The same old tune begins to play,
Chasing all the heavy clouds away.

{c:Chorus 1}

Oh, the merry-go-round keeps turning,
A fire gently burning.
We pass the same familiar trees,
Carried on a steady breeze.
There's comfort in the loops we make,
Every sweet and gentle break.
In the spinning, we are found,
On this joyful merry-go-round.

{c:Verse 2}

Seasons change and the colors fade,
Underneath the canvas shade.
Yet the rhythm holds us tight,
Guiding us through day and night.
The same bright lights, the same sweet air,
No need to rush, no need to care.
Every circle brings us home,
No more a need to wildly roam.

{c:Chorus 2}

Oh, the merry-go-round keeps turning,
A fire gently burning.
We pass the same familiar trees,
Carried on a steady breeze.
There's comfort in the loops we make,
Every sweet and gentle break.
In the spinning, we are found,
On this joyful merry-go-round.

{c:Outro}

Round and round, the music slows,
Where it stops, everybody knows.
Just another turn in store,
Ready for a little more.
Spin again.
Just spin again.
